  "worked_solution": "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(6t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}(0){e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(6(0))-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6(0)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6(0))\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1=2 \\\\ {c}_{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=1.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(6t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
